i_error_status":null,"result":"I'm finishing the review: I checked the plan's claims against `canvasservice.js` and found one factual error.\n\n**What is right:**\n- The core mechanism checks out. Line 1263 `if (requestRes)` counts any acknowledgement as success. Line 1244 turns retry off during shutdown. Lines 1294–1305 put the row back to `SaveVersion`. `shutdown.js:73` waits until no row is in `SaveVersion`.\n- The data-loss finding (T3) is real and valuable.\n- The Executor log is filled in, the follow-up request exists in `.theseus/spawn/` and is listed under Spawned packets, and the diff is within budget and target.\n\n**What is wrong:** for a non-corrupted error, the plan claims the unsaved document is copied to the forgotten-files folder. The code at `canvasservice.js:1306` says otherwise:\n```\nif (storeForgotten && !needRetry && !isEncrypted && (!isError || isErrorCorrupted))\n```\nThe storage copy only runs when there is no error or the error is `CONVERT_CORRUPTED`. Line 1136 has the same guard on the forgotten-files lookup. So:\n- **T4 is wrong:** with a non-corrupted error, no acknowledgement and no retry, no forgotten file is stored today. The test would pin a copy that never happens. The plan's own table in §3 says the same thing for that row (before and after the port), which matters for the human decision. Today that case leaves the edits only in the change log with the row stuck in `SaveVersion`. There is no forgotten-file fallback.\n- **The §3 bullet \"`storeForgotten` + marker can both apply (no ACK case)… Test it\" describes a case that cannot happen.** The new marker only applies to non-corrupted errors, and the forgotten file is only stored for corrupted errors or no error. E4 rests on the same wrong idea, so it has to be reframed: the forgotten file and the marker come from different saves, not the same failure.\n\nThe follow-up characterization packet takes its pins from §4 of this plan, so these errors would carry into the tests, or show up